==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlʊkɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-looking.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊkɪŋ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|look|ing}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|lokinge}}, {{m|enm|lokinde}}, {{m|enm|lokande}}, {{m|enm|lokende}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lōciende}}, present participle of {{der|en|ang|lōcian|t=to look}}, equivalent to {{af|en|look|-ing|id2=participial}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{present participle of|en|look|nocat=1}}
# as the last part of compound adjectives: relating to or having the appearance of.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1935|author=[https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/288354.George_Goodchild George Goodchild]
|title=Death on the Centre Court|chapter=5
|passage=By one o'clock the place was choc-a-bloc. […] The restaurant was packed, and the promenade between the two main courts and the subsidiary courts was thronged with healthy-'''looking''' youngish people, drawn to the Mecca of tennis from all parts of the country.}}
#* '''1988''' September 12, ''New York Magazine'', page 226
#*: Good-'''Looking''', Funny Guy — (Not funny-'''looking''', good guy), 36, Jewish, athletic.
#: ''dorky-'''looking'''''

